# Dark Mode Strategies

## Overview
Tailwind CSS v4 supports class-based dark mode with zero flash.

## 3-Way Strategy

Support light, dark, and system preference.

```html
<html class="light">
```

```css
@variant dark {
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { @slot }
}
```

## Implementation Steps

1. Set initial class via script before paint
```html
<script>
  const theme = localStorage.getItem('theme') || 'system';
  if (theme === 'dark' || (theme === 'system' && matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches)) {
    document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');
  }
  const mq = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)');
  mq.addEventListener('change', () => {
    // Re-evaluate matchMedia directly when theme is system
    if (localStorage.getItem('theme') === 'system') {
      const isDark = mq.matches;
      document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', isDark);
    }
  });
</script>
```

2. Toggle class on user interaction
```ts
function setTheme(mode: 'light' | 'dark' | 'system') {
  localStorage.setItem('theme', mode);
  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', mode === 'dark' || (mode === 'system' && matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches));
}
```

3. Define tokens for both modes
```css
@theme {
  --color-bg: oklch(1 0 0);
  --color-text: oklch(0.15 0 0);
}

.dark {
  --color-bg: oklch(0.15 0 0);
  --color-text: oklch(0.95 0 0);
}
```

## Best Practices

- Use class strategy, not media only
- Apply theme script in `<head>` to prevent FOUC
- Respect `prefers-color-scheme` for system
- Use semantic tokens, not `dark:` utilities everywhere
- Test with forced-colors and high contrast
- For `system` mode, the `@custom-variant dark` variant should be combined with `prefers-color-scheme` when there is no explicit `.light`/`.dark` class.
